  "notes": "Drawn from right-side photos (N295NV and N254NV, 2025) and mirrored for the left; the layout is symmetric. The yellow edging of the orange band changes sides along it (aft at the top, ahead at the bottom), simplified here. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on N295NV: the title runs x 0.141 to 0.319, baseline on the windows' bottoms (y about -0.02), its ascenders 0.42 above (it had been drawn reaching most of the way to the crown), lowercase 0.76 of the ascenders; the sun sits just over the 'gi', centered y 0.5. The band's edges curve gently (an S, steepest near the belly) and are drawn smooth, the yellow strips' square ends kept as corners. The tail sunburst redrawn 2026-11-27 from N320NV (left, side-on): seven rays, placed by eye on the fin as built; the halftone that warms the orange to yellow toward the lower aft corner is drawn as eight stepped tones (a gradient fill would be closer).",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). The year of introduction (2017) is from memory, not a dated source."
